<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- OTHER_STUN_WEAPONS_SURVEY_1 -> owner ruling 2026-08-29: match ION_STUN_IGNORES_BODY_SIZE_1's
     squared standard on the two third-party stun weapons the survey found with a free XML
     lever, rather than settling for vanilla's own linear (1/BodySize) toggle.

     THE MECHANISM, read from Verse.Pawn_HealthTracker.PostApplyDamage, not guessed:
         num *= 1f / pawn.BodySize;                          // victimSeverityScalingByInvBodySize
         num *= pawn.GetStatValue(victimSeverityScaling);    // victimSeverityScaling's StatDef value
     Both apply to the SAME li in sequence, so setting BOTH - the bool AND a StatDef whose own
     value IS 1/BodySize (JawaIonWeapons.Jawa_InverseBodySize, see StatDefs_JawaIon.xml and
     StatPart_InverseBodySize.cs) - multiplies severity by (1/BodySize)^2. No Harmony, no new
     DamageWorker; the owner's squared curve from pure XML on a def we do not own.

     TARGETS, read off guy762.MM.KotORCore's own SpecialDamages.xml / BlasterDamages.xml
     (workshop 3254370945), not the def dump - both currently declare NEITHER field on their
     additionalHediffs li, so PatchOperationAdd cannot collide with an existing value:

         guy762_RangedDamage_KOstun  -> additionalHediffs/li (hediff PsychicShock, severityFixed 10)
         guy762_RangedDamage_sonic   -> additionalHediffs/li (hediff guy762_SonicDisorient, severityPerDamageDealt 0.01)

     Reference humans unaffected by construction: BodySize 1 -> Jawa_InverseBodySize reads 1.0,
     so (1/1)^2 = 1, identical to today. Only the curve away from BodySize 1 changes, same
     invariant the owner's own ruling protected for JawaIon_Damage.

     ⛔ NOT patched: guy762_RangedDamage_organicstun (commented out, dead, in guy762's own
     source), guy762_GrenadeDamage_stun (no additionalHediffs at all - no XML lever exists),
     the whole guy762_*_ion family (survey found these are NOT a flesh-stun mechanism; live-
     tested, ordinary Burn injury on a Rat). See OTHER_STUN_WEAPONS_SURVEY_1.md's table for
     the full per-weapon read.

     MayRequire guy762.MM.KotORCore (this mod's own packageId, read from its About.xml) - the
     whole file is a no-op, not an error, if that mod is inactive.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="guy762.MM.KotORCore">
    <operations>

      <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/DamageDef[defName="guy762_RangedDamage_KOstun"]/additionalHediffs/li</xpath>
        <value>
          <victimSeverityScalingByInvBodySize>true</victimSeverityScalingByInvBodySize>
          <victimSeverityScaling>Jawa_InverseBodySize</victimSeverityScaling>
        </value>
      </li>

      <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/DamageDef[defName="guy762_RangedDamage_sonic"]/additionalHediffs/li</xpath>
        <value>
          <victimSeverityScalingByInvBodySize>true</victimSeverityScalingByInvBodySize>
          <victimSeverityScaling>Jawa_InverseBodySize</victimSeverityScaling>
        </value>
      </li>

    </operations>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
